  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_a304d8323d7d403d85c90cc1562f5e9b",
      "statement": "User preferences are persisted as a single nullable JSON column (`preferences`) on the `auth_users` row in `UserModel` — there is no separate preferences table, and the database imposes no schema on its contents.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/auth/model.py#L26-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c6a301622463896fa1e77bb046d45bf5ddcd9b6fdfc8cfcbbbcd32b8bc429b4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/auth/repository_sqlalchemy.py#L89-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf120138f6e1667975e68bddca7119f47f01401fbb4b840c9c357b6b58463141:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1414ec1c58042049a5f9573f0660d3e",
      "statement": "The backend request model `src.account.api_types.UserPreferences` declares a typed subset of preference keys and sets `extra=\"allow\"`, so a PUT/PATCH body carrying frontend-only keys (holdings_table, holdings_group, drawings, chart_hide_labels, indicator_pane_heights) still validates and is persisted verbatim without a backend change.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/src/lib/api/userPreferencesService.ts#L63-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aebac163f6422fcf5a66443cbd73ed845c4ef9495d1ff3751869909feb689688:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/api_types.py#L84-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8cc17ece535afb73857cfe4ed5e630e3c15a8af6fd63ee4ca735fdf7283f9c8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_adaef6884eb944df93e961b392863b43",
      "statement": "The accounts router exposes GET, PUT and PATCH `/accounts/me/preferences`, all requiring `current_user`; GET returns `{}` when no preferences are stored, PUT replaces the whole blob, and PATCH merges into it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/router.py#L170-L206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e8e40e36e073be6a800e7d4958764ab69bdcc613607ce0e4a256a2a83e622b2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/routers/test_account_unauth.py#L22-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c41d40ff863e6642f3c330ad1bfd11df98afda2e08758472f4e9136d5833260:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a6d69a43e29241ecb8c0d2abfb227071",
      "statement": "Both preference writes call `payload.model_dump(exclude_none=True)` before persisting, so an explicit JSON `null` is dropped rather than stored and is indistinguishable from an omitted field — a client can clear a key only by sending a replacement value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/account/router.py#L181-L206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:968e57aa2590f067a13f0cfcd10062c7360f82edf7bee9836ef472a1fbe39e1f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d36407adef44acab206a62b3ce9fe1b",
      "statement": "PATCH performs a shallow top-level JSONB merge in a single `UPDATE ... RETURNING` using `COALESCE(stored, '{}') || patch`: keys present in the patch are replaced entirely (so sub-objects like `indicators` must be sent whole), keys absent from the patch survive, and the statement returns the fully merged blob.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/auth/repository_sqlalchemy.py#L105-L121",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5605e291c7a829c30512cf16516dd86ea42917bc679eca1ea23fe3bb554e73ae:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/routers/test_accounts.py#L624-L712",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c0894dfa70d2e5bd2a1573f0299517ccf20c99b8c522650aa57fbefa446cd33:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e20310821bd049b39deb50a564692b7e",
      "statement": "Because the JSONB merge is at the top level, concurrent PATCHes to different preference keys survive each other, which is why components across the shell, holdings page, indicator group and drawings service can each write their own key without clobbering others; same-key concurrent writes remain last-writer-wins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/src/lib/components/holdings/holdings-group-prefs.ts#L38-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d350e3cf03a9cdfecd0246d0befc248ea7744b98693b97fcba5d951ad732d101:"
        },
        {
