    {
      "id": "claim_6f397ea39bea470cbf4dbbc874086d4c",
      "statement": "Preferences are non-fatal on every render path: both server loads precompute defaults and wrap the fetch in try/catch, and reading components use optional chaining and shape normalizers, so a failed or malformed preferences request still renders the page with defaults instead of failing the route.",
