      "id": "claim_f430a83ee82b485b978d2613f198d1d3",
      "statement": "Every stored preference value is passed through a shape normalizer rather than trusted: `normalizeHoldingsTableConfig` drops unknown column ids, clamps widths to per-column bounds, restores canonical order and force-keeps the sticky column, while `normalizeHoldingsGroupMode` accepts only explicit `'stock'`/legacy `'company'` and otherwise returns `'none'`.",
      "evidence": [
