      "statement": "The preference contract is pinned by tests at both ends: the Rust-side router tests in `tests/routers/test_accounts.py` cover empty-store defaults, PUT round trips, PATCH partial merges and cross-component merge survival, and per-key round trips for every shipped key; the Vitest suites cover request method/path/body shapes, `tokenOverride`, empty-`{}` responses, and the default fallback path when preferences reject.",
